# THE LAST HOUR: PROJECT ECHO — MERGED NORMAL-PROGRESSION BUILD (v187)
# Includes the main menu, identity/computer introduction, outdoor approach, laboratory puzzles,
# Security Room sequence, final ECHO challenges, and the escape ending.
# v187: Removed hidden progression bypass keys, admin/debug shortcuts, and the H hitbox toggle.
# v186: The Main Exit reveals the exterior as it opens; stronger ending glitch and a late escape fade.
# v185: Brighter flashlight; white PROJECT ECHO ending title followed by a full-screen signal glitch-out.
# v177: Hard Security Room perimeter enforcement prevents wall clipping at all movement speeds.
# Fixes Security Room entry snapping by separating Security and Observation Room movement bounds.
# Adds continuous final-sequence objectives, cyan world waypoints, and waypoint audio pings.
# Keeps the three required minigames in sequence and retains the exit cutscene/title card.

# v149: Use the user-provided recorded door slam for the cinematic impacts.
# v161: Remove the unintended Research Room humanoid silhouette; darken the far-room mask; make both door leaves launch toward and past the player on the first blast frame.
# v150: Slower door-breach pacing.
# v151: Camera arcs around the workstation instead of entering the monitor; the second impact caves the handle area in with a smooth concave mesh. Ends here for visual approval.
# THE LAST HOUR: PROJECT ECHO — MAIN LAB + SECURITY + ELECTRICITY SHELL
# v155: Fire the third recorded door bang before switching to the visible cave-in state, synchronizing sound and deformation.
# v125: High-contrast dark monitor palette with bright readable white/cyan/amber text; eliminate washed-out pale UI.
# v117: Phase 5 archive module pickup, upgraded Main Lab CPU/microphone, terminal boot/menu, and ECHO conversation stopping at "We will see."
# v116: Hollow reinforced archive locker shell, detailed visible interior shelving/contents, and detailed swinging door faces.
# Observation doorway late-pass + dark frame/infill + expanded Research header cover v64.
# v75: Main Lab lever snap + 5-second lighting failure, spark burst, power-loss terminal and scaled workstation
# THE LAST HOUR — Main Lab + Security Room + Electricity Room v9
# OBSERVATION INTERIOR HALF-TURN v65: inner contents/window rotate 180 degrees; Main Lab doorway remains fixed.
# RUNTIME STATE INITIALIZATION FIX v17: restores omitted Main Lab door, movement, UI, and switch-timer defaults.
# Adds the standalone-v38 Console A/B/C minigames and Auxiliary Induction Tube collectible only.
# Adds hitboxes and integrated generator recovery: tube install, induction alignment, coolant, pressure, startup.
# MEMORY WAVE CALIBRATION UI v36: isolated three-channel waveform interface and matching hitboxes.
# OBSERVATION ENTRANCE CLEARANCE v40: stale relocated-prop hitboxes fixed; blank infill panel removed permanently.
# OBSERVATION ROOM v43 FIX: registers missing cone helper and centralizes door alignment; preserves v42 furniture and v40 doorway clearance.
# OBSERVATION WEST DOOR CENTERED v37: relocates doorway and clears/reuses its former wall bay.
# Retains all four wall phases, fire-extinguisher fix, and camera culling. Labels the three secured doors; the south Main Lab entrance and smaller west-wall Security opening remain open.
# Main Menu and Pathway remain isolated out; existing story, pickups, puzzles and door interactions are retained.
# v102: stand-clear reach/return arc, persistent live tracking head, and more visible two-pass scan sweep.
# v106: Research Room south-exit black-outside shader mask and jump camera pitch preservation.
# v107: Post-awakening ECHO signal notice, Observation Room access unlock, and investigation waypoint.
# v108: Keep the robot cutscene active through a single terminal access message; add a 15-second Observation Room explore objective.
# v135: Skip the Beat 1 robot CCTV/security flash and flow directly into Beat 2; redesign both failed-transfer report pages as clean aged-paper documents.
# v137: Expand the Beat 2 report into four distinct accident dossier files; E advances files and the final file returns to the crimson ECHO screen.
# v138: Stronger near-black ink, a darker parchment tone, bold document typography, larger entry text, and concise incident lines for reliable readability on the in-world CRT.

# OBSERVATION DOORWAY ANGLE-SNAG FIX v73: adds a narrow fully-open portal crossing path to prevent diagonal jamb/collider snags; leaves room collision intact.
# v162: Latch-fragment contact immediately drops the camera to the floor/ceiling view.
# v182: Upgrades final-boss terminal with blueprint grid, telemetry sidecars, dashboard tiles, animated signals, and hover feedback.
# v166: Adds the alternate ECHO termination route, three interactive workstation puzzles,
# main-exit passage release, and the ending card.
# v183: Stage the Main Exit shot (camera aims at closed door, door opens, hold, run, late fade).
# v180: Fix Research-vs-Security room-bound overlap that snapped players at the Security cupboards; keep swept physical collision and locker collider.
# v178: swept wall collision plus a hard Security Room interior envelope and a doorway-only corridor;
# prevents sidestepping through the Main Lab/Security wall overlap or clipping through perimeter walls.
# Renderer is the uploaded Pyray/Raylib v165 build (not an Ursina runtime).
